    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Speak of deadly cold, and I think of polar explorers. I was "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "skeptical",
            "zh": "怀疑的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " when Damian Bailey, from the University of South Wales, invited me to take part in a cold experiment at 10 degrees Celsius. “It sounds "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "mild",
            "ref": "v-mild"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", but it’s a real challenge,” he told me."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I was led into the environmental room. The plan was to start at 21 degrees Celsius, lower the temperature to 10 degrees, and record how my body would respond. "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " I was still "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "unaware",
            "ref": "v-unaware"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of the big changes inside my body, but there were already "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "signs",
            "ref": "v-sign"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " on the outside. When the room dropped to 18 degrees, the hairs on my arms stood up to help "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "insulate",
            "zh": "把……隔绝起来"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " my body. “Science tells us that 18 degrees is the tipping point. The body is now working to keep your core at around 37 degrees,” Bailey explained."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " The "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "blood vessels",
            "zh": "血管"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in my hands were constricting to keep my warm blood flowing to my major "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "organs",
            "ref": "v-organ"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". This would happen even faster if I were the opposite sex, Bailey said. "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " I felt uncomfortable as we repeated all the measurements. It soon became clear I was wrong to doubt that 10 degrees would affect me."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "What shocked me was the change in blood flow to the brain and how much longer it took me to complete a shape-sorting game. But my body was achieving its main goal of keeping my core at around 37 degrees—it just had to work harder. "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " My blood pressure was shooting up while my blood was thickening. That’s why heart attacks are more common in the winter."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Bailey suggests we all heat our rooms to around 18 degrees in winter. If that is not possible, wear warm clothing. "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Do not just sit in a chair and watch TV."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "label": "I",
      "instruction": "Fill in each blank in the article with a proper sentence given below. Each sentence can be used only once. Note that there are two more sentences than you will need.",
      "bank": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "My heart was beating faster."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Next, my fingers turned white."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "At 10 degrees, the fans stopped."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Try to produce extra body heat by moving around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "E",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "After the first measurements were taken, the fans started working."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "F",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "I wouldn’t want to be trying to do school homework in such a cold room."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "G",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Ten degrees is the average temperature that people will be living in if they can’t afford to heat their homes."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
